node_modules
.wrangler
.dev.vars
# The bridge WASM and its wasm-bindgen glue are build output, not source.
# They are produced by `npm run build:wasm`, which drives
# ../aexeo-emdash/scripts/build-wasm.sh against this directory, and are
# committed nowhere: a checked-in .wasm goes stale silently, and the
# hand-written .d.ts files get edited to match the stale binary instead of
# the plugin that actually calls it. Same reasoning, and the same carve-out,
# as ../aexeo-emdash/.gitignore.
#
# Named patterns rather than `src/wasm/*`, because src/wasm/init.ts is
# ordinary source: a directory-wide rule would ignore it too, and the
# exception list would then have to grow every time real code lands there.
#
# The two `.d.ts` files ARE tracked: they are the contract this package's
# TypeScript compiles against. wasm-bindgen does not emit `_bg.d.ts` for the
# bundler target at all, and the `.wasm.d.ts` has to describe a precompiled
# WebAssembly.Module rather than the ESM export shape wasm-bindgen would
# assume. Keep them in step with ../aexeo-emdash/wasm/ when the bridge
# surface changes.
src/wasm/*.wasm
src/wasm/*.js
src/wasm/*.wasm-bindgen
